{
 "popseq_schema": "1.0.0",
 "generated": "2026-11-09",
 "what": "One static JSON file per fungal species with 100 or more isolates. Each holds the full description of the species and a pre-selected panel of up to 100 strains to profile.",
 "scope": "public whole-genome Illumina, BGISEQ and DNBSEQ sequencing runs of fungal isolates, as ENA and NCBI describe them",
 "archive_snapshot": "2026-11-06",
 "richer_queries": {
  "command": "uv run popseq",
  "python": "import popseq; popseq.panel(taxid=746128, n=100)",
  "mcp": "uv run --extra mcp python -m popseq.mcp_server (stdio)",
  "static_json": "catalog/api/index.json and catalog/api/<taxid>.json, fetchable over raw.githubusercontent.com with no clone",
  "legacy_command": "uv run python scripts/popseq_query.py (shim)",
  "verbs": {
   "species": "list species with counts; the discovery entry point",
   "runs": "all runs of one species, filtered",
   "panel": "select N strains, one per isolate, spread across studies",
   "describe": "everything known about one species, as JSON"
  },
  "exit_codes": {
   "0": "ok",
   "2": "species not found or ambiguous",
   "3": "filters left nothing"
  },
  "stable": "Verb names, flag names and the JSON key names are the contract. Table paths and columns may change underneath."
 },
 "caveats": [
  "Every count is a floor. ENA holds runs with an empty tax_id that no taxonomy query reaches, so the true per-species totals are higher (issue #2).",
  "A run count is not a strain count and an isolate count is not an independent-sample count. 52 of the 113 largest species take half or more of their isolates from one study. Read catalog/summary/clonality.csv.gz before treating a species as a population.",
  "est_depth_x comes from metadata, not from the reads.",
  "Only 113 species were reconciled against NCBI. For every other species ncbi_status is not_checked, which is not the same as absent.",
  "Nothing here has been downloaded or verified. These are archive records.",
  "Scope: the run table holds only ENA runs with library_strategy=WGS and library_source=GENOMIC, on instrument_platform ILLUMINA (snapshot 2026-11-06) or BGISEQ/DNBSEQ (supplement 2026-11-09; scripts/popseq_snapshot.py). A --strategy filter for anything else returns nothing because those runs were never harvested, not because none exist (issue #24). The --platform filter defaults to ILLUMINA; pass BGISEQ, DNBSEQ or '' to see the others."
 ],
